  "body": "## What changed\n- Added `crates/post/src/post/g93.rs` implementing the shared Rust `G93` inverse-time feed solver (`F = 1 / dt_min`, `min^-1`).\n- Computed `dt_cut = ||tip_1 - tip_0|| / v_prog` in part space, computed `dt_lim` from stated linear (`X/Y/Z` `mm/min`) and rotary (`A/B/C` `deg/min`) `max_normal_speed` limits, and took `dt_min = max(dt_cut, dt_lim)`.\n- Handled pure rotary reorientations (`ds_tip <= eps`) using configured `rotary_only_deg_per_min`, stated axis limits, or `v_prog` fallback without division by zero, and skipped zero-motion duplicate moves (`G93Decision::Skip`).\n- Clamped finite `F` to `f_min..=f_max` (`0.001..=60_000.0`), floor-formatted `F` words to 4 decimals (`format_g93_feed_word`), refused invalid feeds, limits, or options by name, and verified `G20` (inch) vs `G21` (mm) unit invariance.\n- Re-exported `g93` APIs from `crates/post/src/post/mod.rs`, `crates/post/src/post/rotary_cap.rs`, and `crates/post/src/kinematics/mod.rs`.\n- Added `crates/post/src/post/section_mode.rs` and `crates/app/src/posting_section_mode.rs`, and wired `section_mode::insert` into `crates/app/src/posting.rs` to emit `PARAM SectionMode` (`\"3-axis\"`, `\"3+2 indexed\"`, `\"simultaneous 5-axis\"`) per milling operation stream.\n\n## Cause\n- Multi-axis post work (#1958, #1968, #1969) needed a shared `G93` inverse-time feed solver honoring linear/rotary `max_normal_speed` limits without division by zero, and explicit `.cnc` section mode metadata distinguishing `3-axis`, `3+2 indexed`, and `simultaneous 5-axis` streams without altering legacy `.cl` inputs, `Dump::default()`, or 3-axis `.nc` output.\n\n## Tests\n- **Pin `g93_feed`** (`crates/post/tests/g93_feed.rs`, 5 tests): Failed compilation before fix (`unresolved import camcraft_post::post::g93`); passes after final edit (`5 passed; 0 failed`).\n- **Pin `section_mode`** (`crates/app/tests/section_mode.rs`, 2 tests): Failed assertion before fix (`left: None, right: Some(\"3-axis\")`); passes after final edit (`2 passed; 0 failed`).\n- **Unit tests**: `camcraft-post --lib` (`64 passed; 0 failed`) and `camcraft-app --lib section_mode` (`1 passed; 0 failed`).\n- **Mutation checks**:\n  - Disabled `dt_lim` maxing in `g93.rs`: `g93_feed` failed (`2 failed`), passed when restored.\n  - Disabled zero-motion `Skip` guard in `g93.rs`: `g93_feed` failed (`1 failed`), passed when restored.\n  - Removed `f_min..=f_max` clamp in `g93.rs`: `g93_feed` failed (`1 failed`), passed when restored.\n  - Removed `section_mode::insert` in `posting.rs`: `section_mode` failed (`1 failed`), passed when restored.\n  - Disabled `params.tilt().is_some()` check in `posting_section_mode.rs`: `section_mode` failed (`1 failed`), passed when restored.\n- **Clippy & Gate**:\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green (`0` warnings).\n  - `cargo run --package xtask -- gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (`post suites` 27s + `app suites` 1463s, `0 failed`).\n\n## Goldens moved\n- None (`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty).\n\n## Not exercised\n- `.cps` post-processor G93 emission (`mach4.cps`, `haas.cps`) and UI checkbox/toggle wiring belong to downstream issues (#1968, #1969) and were not modified here.\n\n## Overlaps\n- Touches different lines/functions in `crates/app/src/posting.rs` and/or `crates/post/src/post/mod.rs` from open PRs #468, #1681, #2115, #2136, #2149, #2162; whichever merges second refreshes. Checked with `git merge-tree --write-tree upstream/main HEAD` (`1b6e08182`): zero conflicts.\n\nChangelog: Added shared G93 inverse-time feed solver and explicit SectionMode markers (3-axis, 3+2 indexed, simultaneous 5-axis) in post streams.\n\nFixes #1966\n",
